# Root build context — used by engine/apps/api/Dockerfile, which must build
# from the repo root to reach its local path dependencies (now-config,
# now-rails). Without this file the context is gigabytes: ~280 MB of
# WordPress dumps, ~330 MB of extracted content JSONL, every .venv and
# node_modules in the tree, and the whole .git history.
#
# Deny-by-default is not used here because the api build legitimately needs
# three directories from different parts of the tree; an explicit deny list
# keeps that readable.

# VCS and tooling
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Dependency trees — reinstalled inside the image from lockfiles
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/.next
# And the alternate build dirs NEXT_DIST_DIR can produce during parallel
# work. `**/.next` does not match `.next-a`, so without this a local
# `docker build` sends someone's in-progress build output as context.
**/.next-*

# Secrets: never in a build context. A COPY . would bake these into a layer
# that survives in the image even if a later step deletes them.
.env
**/.env
!**/.env.example
**/secrets/

# Production data and anything derived from it (docs/data-provenance.md).
# None of it belongs in an application image. The city trees are ~300 MB
# each, almost entirely dumps and extracted JSONL.
*/db/
*/content/
*/cms/
backups/
media_mirror_state/

# jakarta/site and bali/site are small and ARE config the apps may read
# (brand tokens, taxonomy mapping, place-overrides), so they stay.

# Local infrastructure state
engine/infra/garage/data
engine/infra/garage/meta

# Docs and scratch — no effect on a build, only on context size
*.md
docs/
!engine/apps/api/README.md
